<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">12 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 12 February, from 1502 to 1974.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1502">1502 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">524 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Castile orders its Muslims to convert or leave</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A decree of Isabella I gave the Muslims of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> a choice between baptism and exile. Most converted, becoming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moriscos">Moriscos</a>, whose descendants were expelled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1609-14.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moriscos">Moriscos</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1541">1541 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">485 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pedro de Valdivia founds Santiago in Chile</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Spanish conquistador <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-valdivia">Pedro de Valdivia</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> in the central valley at the foot of the Andes. It became the seat of the governors of Chile and, from 1609, of its royal audiencia.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-valdivia">Pedro de Valdivia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1554">1554 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">472 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lady Jane Grey is executed at the Tower</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The teenage Protestant queen, deposed after nine days in 1553, was beheaded on Mary I's orders following Wyatt's Rebellion. Her husband Guildford Dudley was executed the same morning.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1809">1809 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">217 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Abraham Lincoln is born in Kentucky</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Born in a one-room log cabin near Hodgenville, Lincoln was largely self-taught. As the 16th President he led the Union through the Civil War and helped bring about the end of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1809">1809 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">217 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles Darwin is born in Shrewsbury</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Born on the same day as Lincoln, Darwin sailed on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hms-beagle">HMS Beagle</a> and developed the theory of evolution by natural selection, published in '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/on-the-origin-of-species">On the Origin of Species</a>' in 1859.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1818">1818 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">208 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Chile proclaims its independence from Spain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernardo-ohiggins">Bernardo O'Higgins</a> formally proclaimed Chile's independence on the first anniversary of the victory at Chacabuco. Spanish forces were decisively beaten at Maipú that April.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1912">1912 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">114 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Puyi, the last Emperor of China, abdicates</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Empress Dowager Longyu issued the edict of abdication for the six-year-old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puyi">Puyi</a>. The fall of the Qing ended more than two thousand years of imperial rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1974">1974 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">52 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet authorities arrest Aleksandr Solzhenitsyn</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Weeks after 'The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulag">Gulag</a> Archipelago' appeared in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, the Nobel laureate was arrested in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> and charged with treason. The next day he was stripped of citizenship and deported to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 12 February <span class="n">9</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-henry-margrave-of-moravia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-henry-margrave-of-moravia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Henry, Margrave of Moravia</span><span class="tp">1322–1375</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/giovanni-ii-bentivoglio"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/giovanni-ii-bentivoglio.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Giovanni II Bentivoglio</span><span class="tp">1443–1508</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-of-legnica"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-ii-of-legnica.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Frederick II of Legnica</span><span class="tp">1480–1547</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-winthrop-the-younger"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-winthrop-the-younger.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Winthrop the Younger</span><span class="tp">1606–1676</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-darwin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-darwin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles Darwin</span><span class="tp">1809–1882</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abraham-lincoln.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Abraham Lincoln</span><span class="tp">1809–1865</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/thubten-gyatso"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/thubten-gyatso.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Thubten Gyatso</span><span class="tp">1876–1933</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/walter-nash"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/walter-nash.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Walter Nash</span><span class="tp">1882–1968</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/johan-laidoner"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johan-laidoner.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Johan Laidoner</span><span class="tp">1884–1953</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 12 February <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/benedict-of-aniane"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/benedict-of-aniane.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Benedict of Aniane</span><span class="tp">c. 747–821</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/catherine-of-navarre"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/catherine-of-navarre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Catherine of Navarre</span><span class="tp">1468–1517</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/adolf-frederick-king-of-sweden"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/adolf-frederick-king-of-sweden.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Adolf Frederick, King of Sweden</span><span class="tp">1710–1771</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ethan-allen"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ethan-allen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ethan Allen</span><span class="tp">1738–1789</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/immanuel-kant"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/immanuel-kant.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Immanuel Kant</span><span class="tp">1724–1804</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hans-von-bulow"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hans-von-bulow.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hans von Bülow</span><span class="tp">1830–1894</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lillie-langtry"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lillie-langtry.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lillie Langtry</span><span class="tp">1853–1929</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/julio-cortazar"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/julio-cortazar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Julio Cortázar</span><span class="tp">1914–1984</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
